  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Cap Ghir</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.worldcat.org/title/itineraria-phoenicia/oclc/474792195\">Lipinski</a> identifies the Braca mountains as the western slopes of the High <a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"../846\" title=\"Atlas Mon(te)s\">Atlas</a> range where it meets the <a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"../845\" title=\"Atlanticus Oceanus\">Atlantic</a> Ocean.\u00a0</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A mountain on the northwest coast of Africa mentioned by the Elder Pliny that is probably to be identified with the western slopes of the Atlas range.",
